{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966479,"nonce":"D+XS/OT9NvVJUvMaV9BfX8GnDqU=","title":"TextInput cursor lands in the wrong place after a window resize","message":"Clicking into a `text_input` after the window has been resized puts the\ncaret somewhere other than where the click landed.\n\n`crates/blinc_layout/src/widgets/text_input.rs` stores layout bounds for\nits scroll calculation. A resize does not refresh them, so the\nclick-to-cursor mapping converts against stale geometry.\n\nRepro: open any text_input demo, resize the window, click into the field.\n\nCarried over from the root `backlog.md`, which this issue replaces.","files":null}]}